\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par  \cf0 1. Wait, my soul, and tarry,
\par \pard\li225\sl180\slmult0 Tarry with God!
\par He will help thee carry
\par Ev'ry grievous load
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Why fret and fear
\par When the morn is near?
\par With the passing winter
\par Spring will re-appear.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par When storms distress thee,
\par In ev'ry ill
\par God will surely bless thee,
\par My soul, be still.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2. Wait my soul, and tarry,
\par \pard\li225\sl180\slmult0 Tarry with God!
\par He will help thee carry
\par Ev'ry grievous load.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par When all things fail,
\par God will still prevail.
\par He can safely lead thee
\par Thro' the darkest vale.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Lord, God eternal,
\par Lead to the goal!
\par Christ, for ever faithful,
\par Save thou my soul!
\par \pard\li315\sl180\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3. Wait my soul, and tarry,
\par \pard\li315\sl180\slmult0 Tarry with God!
\par He will help thee carry
\par Ev'ry grievous load.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par When life shall cease,
\par God will grant release.
\par Out of sorrow lead me
\par Into blessed peace.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par When thro' affliction
\par Thy way I've trod,
\par Follows joy eternal,
\par \pard      Thou faithful God!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

